course: dictionary
lesson: 902
title: Bitterly: hurt, harsh and very strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Peter went outside and wept bitterly.» Wept means cried. The word bitterly tells you how he cried: in a hurt, unhappy way, after he had let his friend down. The words around it are the clues.
explain: «The hills were bitterly cold this January.» Here bitterly does not mean sad at all. It means very, or extremely, cold. Check it by swapping in very: «very cold» still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Bitterly is also used with strong feelings, like «bitterly disappointed» or «bitterly regret». These mean the feeling was deep and strong. In the story about Chloe, «seven-year-olds in a temper do things they bitterly regret» means they really, deeply wish they had not done them.
fact: Bitterly means in an angry, hurt and unhappy way.
fact: Bitterly can also mean very or extremely, as in «bitterly cold».
fact: Bitterly can show very strong feelings, as in «bitterly disappointed», «bitterly regret» or «bitterly complained».
fact: In history and the news, «bitterly fought» means fought fiercely, with great anger.
fact: To check the meaning, swap in a simpler word such as very, sad or strongly, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The hills were bitterly cold this January.» What does bitterly mean here? | Late at night | *Very, extremely | Warm and sunny | Gently and softly
exercise: «Ella was bitterly disappointed when the match was cancelled.» What does bitterly show? | Mild interest | Silly joy | *Very strong hurt and unhappiness | Happy relief
exercise: «He wept bitterly after the loss.» Find and copy the word that tells you he was crying. | *wept | he | after | loss
test: Nadia says bitterly is just another way of saying sadly. Why might an author choose bitterly instead? | It means happy | It is a longer word | It means exactly the same as sadly, so there is no reason to pick it | *It shows the feeling was deep, angry and hurt, not just a little sad
test: Which phrase uses bitterly to mean very cold? | happily cold | gently cold | *bitterly cold | quietly cold
exam: Lena says «bitterly disappointed» means slightly sad. Is she right? | Yes, it means a little bit sad | No, it means very cold | Yes, it means happy and calm | *No, it means very strongly disappointed and hurt
